  "configuration_id": "config_033",
  "reason": "The current best is config_006 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, transformer) at 0.653 accuracy. The key remaining question is whether adding image features to this strong RNA baseline can push accuracy higher. Image-only is weak (0.208), but complementary information in multimodal fusion is not guaranteed to be absent. Config_033 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, weighted) is the most direct extension of our best result, isolating the effect of adding the image modality while keeping the proven RNA encoder, multiprofile setting, and transformer aggregation. Weighted fusion is preferred over concat because the image modality is substantially weaker, and weighted fusion allows the model to downweight the less informative signal. This is the highest-value experiment: if it beats 0.653, we have a new best and a direction to refine; if it doesn't, we confirm RNA-only multiprofile is the ceiling and can spend remaining budget on minor refinements."
}

